Fix a game $G$, a repetition count $n$, a strategy $S$ for $G^{n}$, a coordinate set $D$ with strictly positive postselection mass $p_D$, and a parameter $\eta\in\mathbb{R}$. Suppose the fair operator entropy bound at level $\eta$ holds, i.e. Alice's accepted operator entropy and Bob's accepted operator entropy relative to $D$ are both at most $2p_D\eta$. Then the source-state distance bound at level $\eta$ holds: writing $
u$ for the postselected locally sampleable law and $\gamma_t,\psi_t,\phi_t$ for its three associated families of unit vectors,
$$\sum_{t}
u(t)\,\lVert\gamma_t-\psi_tVert^{2}\le 8\eta\qquad	ext{and}\qquad\sum_{t}
u(t)\,\lVert\psi_t-\phi_tVert^{2}\le 8\eta.$$
So an entropy budget of $2p_D\eta$ on each side forces the three families of source states to agree to within $8\eta$ on average, with the postselection mass no longer appearing.
